  "_narrative": "**Where We Stand**\nWe are at the starting line in Pool B with a clean slate of 0 points. Our path forward is clear: out of 729 possible combinations of outcomes in the pool, we advance in 309 of them.\n\n**Our Next Game**\nWe take the ice for our tournament opener against the Nepean Wildcats today, Friday, Oct 16, at 2:15 PM. Every shift matters as we look to secure our first points of the weekend.\n\n**Around the Pool**\nPool B action begins at 12:30 PM with Wilmot Wolverine facing the Belmont Blazers. We will follow that result closely as we prepare for our own debut this afternoon.",
  "_coaches_corner": {
    "don_cherry": "Now look at this right here\u2014those Kanata Rangers girls are ready to go! Ranked eighteen? Forget that, it\u2019s all about HEART and working your socks off! You backcheck, you protect your tender, and you play for the girl beside you\u2014BEAUTIES! Double thumbs up, let\u2019s go!",
    "talking_points": "**Mindset**\nWe are starting this tournament with a completely clean slate, which gives us the perfect opportunity to establish our identity right from the opening whistle. Let\u2019s channel our pre-game energy into a fast start and set a high standard for how the Kanata Rangers play hockey.\n\n**The Opponent**\nThe Nepean Wildcats are a disciplined, hardworking team that will capitalize if we lose our focus or take shifts off. We need to respect their speed through the neutral zone and ensure we are winning the individual battles along the boards to take away their time and space.\n\n**What We Need**\nWith only the top seed in the pool advancing, these first two points are critical for our path to the quarterfinals. We need to play a complete team game and remain mindful of our defensive zone, as goal differential can often be the deciding factor in such a tight tournament format."
  }
